# MVX account descriptor
name = mv_package
version = 1

# THE VENDOR PERMIT.  It binds at the RESTRICTED tier only for the exact program
# the system layer has blessed (build.sh writes that hash), so an account cannot
# grant itself these commands by editing this file -- the name has to match a
# blessing it cannot forge.
#
# This lived in .mv-account until #183, which mvx does not read grants from, so
# it had never bound at all: MVPKG needed the unrestricted tier to do what this
# line was supposed to allow at the restricted one.
#
# ldd: the load check (MVPKGOS LDCHECK) asks the shipped file which libraries it
# needs, because the clibs a package DECLARES describe what its source links and
# not what the prebuilt in the artifact was linked against (#177).  Read-only,
# argv-style, and the install behaves exactly as it did before this grant if it
# is absent -- an ungranted check answers "cannot tell", never "missing".
permit prog:MVPKG = mkdir rmtree untar mkpkg chown ldd
